During the 1968–69 Scottish football season, [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] competed in [[Scottish Division One]].

Celtic won the [[Treble (association football)|domestic treble]] for only the second time in their history, as well as the second time in three seasons. They won the League for the fourth year in a row, as well as the League Cup for the fourth time in a row, which was a record at the time. With this treble, Celtic reached 50 major domestic honours.

